## What the PDS is

The Property Development Scheme is one of the routes the Economic Development Board (EDB) approves for selling homes to foreigners. A PDS project is built on freehold land of at least one arpent (0.4220 hectare) and has at least six homes. It must include public spaces and leisure or commercial amenities open to the community plus day to day services for residents such as security and maintenance and gardening.

## Who can buy

A Mauritian citizen or a foreign national or a member of the Mauritian diaspora. Also companies and sociétés and limited partnerships and trusts with a qualified trustee and foundations.

## What you can buy

- Villas and apartments and penthouses and similar homes with services and amenities.
- Serviced plots of land of up to 2 100 m² on which you build your own house.

There is no minimum price for a home under the PDS. Apart from apartments and penthouses each plot of land for a house can be up to 5 276 m².

## Residency

Buying a home for **USD 375 000 or more** gives you a residence permit for as long as you own it. Your spouse and your children under 24 get one too. With this permit you do not need an occupation or work permit to invest and work in Mauritius.

If you buy a serviced plot the residence permit only comes once the house on it is finished. A foreign buyer must build within five years and can buy only one plot. They can only do so if they already hold a residence or occupation or permanent residence permit.

## How you pay

- Foreign buyers pay in US dollars or another freely convertible currency with money brought in from abroad through a reputable bank.
- If you take a loan in rupees with a bank in Mauritius the first USD 500 000 must still be paid in foreign currency.
- Off plan the price is paid in stages as the building goes up: 25% when you sign and 10% after the foundations. Then 35% when the building is roofed and 25% on completion and 5% when the home is handed over.

## Costs on top of the price

- **Registration duty**: 5% of the price paid by the buyer (also on a resale).
- **Land transfer tax**: 5% paid by the seller when a home is resold.
- **EDB processing fee**: MUR 25 000 per application not refundable.
- Notary fees: ask your notary for a written quote.

## Renting it out and selling

You can rent your home out through the PDS company or the property manager it appoints. You can sell at any price to a foreigner or a Mauritian or a company. You must tell the EDB in writing at least 30 days before the sale.

